00:08:16.729 --> 00:08:18.931
November of 20, 22.

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:21.367
So it would have absolutely overlapped

00:08:21.367 --> 00:08:22.869
with the election itself.

00:08:22.869 --> 00:08:24.537
I hesitate to use this term,

00:08:24.537 --> 00:08:25.204
but I can't think of one

00:08:25.204 --> 00:08:26.072
better on the moment.

00:08:26.072 --> 00:08:27.840
This is javy stuff

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:30.009
when you're raising money in a campaign.

00:08:30.009 --> 00:08:31.777
The one thing you know

00:08:31.777 --> 00:08:32.211
when you

00:08:32.211 --> 00:08:33.779
raise money for a campaign is

00:08:33.779 --> 00:08:35.948
you can't spend campaign money

00:08:35.948 --> 00:08:37.183
on personal stuff.

00:08:37.183 --> 00:08:38.718
Yeah.
It's remarkably

00:08:38.718 --> 00:08:40.620
in some sense unsophisticated.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:42.488
I mean there's all we've seen politicians

00:08:42.488 --> 00:08:43.022
over the years

00:08:43.022 --> 00:08:45.024
sort of in more sophisticated ways

00:08:45.024 --> 00:08:45.558
launder money.

00:08:45.558 --> 00:08:47.126
Maybe that'll come into play here.

00:08:47.126 --> 00:08:47.960
But use it in ways

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.095
where maybe it's arguable.

00:08:49.095 --> 00:08:50.363
Is this a campaign expenses?

00:08:50.363 --> 00:08:51.264
It's a personal expense,

00:08:51.264 --> 00:08:53.332
but the things that Caitlin just laid out

00:08:53.332 --> 00:08:53.866
that are laid out in

00:08:53.866 --> 00:08:54.300
the indictment

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.536
are seemingly undoubtedly

00:08:56.769 --> 00:08:57.737
personal expenses.

00:08:57.737 --> 00:08:59.138
So if prosecutors can prove that,

00:08:59.138 --> 00:08:59.939
by the way,

00:09:00.339 --> 00:09:01.974
prosecutors are going to be very careful

00:09:01.974 --> 00:09:02.808
before they bring a charge

00:09:02.808 --> 00:09:04.143
against a sitting member of Congress.

00:09:04.143 --> 00:09:05.511
So if they can prove that,

00:09:05.511 --> 00:09:06.145
then then

00:09:06.145 --> 00:09:07.980
that'll make out the wire fraud claims.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.649
And you made the point

00:09:09.649 --> 00:09:11.551
that this has happened fairly fast

00:09:11.551 --> 00:09:13.719
so that, you know the evidence

00:09:13.719 --> 00:09:14.587
they have to have it

00:09:14.587 --> 00:09:15.454
in order to go forward

00:09:15.454 --> 00:09:16.756
with this obviously,

00:09:16.756 --> 00:09:17.790
they've got paperwork

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:18.691
and we will have to see.

00:09:18.691 --> 00:09:20.426
We do have something now

00:09:20.426 --> 00:09:21.661
coming out from the court.

00:09:21.661 --> 00:09:23.996
Brynn Gingras is joining us now live.

00:09:24.297 --> 00:09:25.565
She's got an update for us

00:09:25.565 --> 00:09:27.166
a statement, I understand, from the DOJ

00:09:30.136 --> 00:09:31.237
Yeah, that's right.

00:09:31.237 --> 00:09:31.971
Sara, we

00:09:31.971 --> 00:09:33.372
learned that the grand jury returned

00:09:33.372 --> 00:09:34.574
this indictment yesterday,

00:09:34.574 --> 00:09:36.275
and now we have this 13

00:09:36.275 --> 00:09:37.710
count indictment, a statement.

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:38.878
I want to read it in full to you.

00:09:38.878 --> 00:09:39.478
It's quite long.

00:09:39.478 --> 00:09:39.779
It says,

00:09:39.779 --> 00:09:40.913
This indictment seeks

00:09:40.913 --> 00:09:42.815
to hold Santos accountable

00:09:42.815 --> 00:09:44.083
for various alleged

00:09:44.083 --> 00:09:45.151
fraudulent schemes

00:09:45.151 --> 00:09:47.286
and brazen misrepresentations.

00:09:47.286 --> 00:09:48.421
Taken together,

00:09:48.421 --> 00:09:50.122
the allegations in the indictment

00:09:50.122 --> 00:09:50.957
charge Santos

00:09:50.957 --> 00:09:52.491
with relying on repeated

00:09:52.491 --> 00:09:54.160
dishonesty and deception

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.362
to ascend to the halls of Congress

00:09:56.362 --> 00:09:57.697
and enrich himself.

00:09:57.697 --> 00:09:59.398
He used political contributions

00:09:59.398 --> 00:10:00.733
to line his pockets,

00:10:00.733 --> 00:10:02.101
unlawfully applied

00:10:02.101 --> 00:10:03.002
for unemployment

00:10:03.002 --> 00:10:04.303
benefits that should have gone

00:10:04.303 --> 00:10:06.272
to New Yorkers who had lost their jobs

00:10:06.272 --> 00:10:07.740
due to the pandemic

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:09.976
and lied to the House of Representatives.

00:10:10.209 --> 00:10:11.043
My office

00:10:11.043 --> 00:10:12.645
and our law enforcement partners

00:10:12.645 --> 00:10:13.245
will continue

00:10:13.245 --> 00:10:14.580
to aggressively root out

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:16.048
corruption and self-dealing

00:10:16.048 --> 00:10:18.284
from our communities, public institutions

00:10:18.284 --> 00:10:19.685
and hold public officials

00:10:19.685 --> 00:10:21.787
accountable to the constituents

00:10:21.787 --> 00:10:22.922
who elected them.

00:10:22.922 --> 00:10:25.291
And of course, he went into office

00:10:25.358 --> 00:10:26.726
just in January.

00:10:26.726 --> 00:10:28.427
But we know that the investigation

00:10:28.427 --> 00:10:29.362
into him

00:10:29.362 --> 00:10:31.697
where before that my colleague Mark

00:10:31.697 --> 00:10:33.265
Morales, is learning from sources

00:10:33.265 --> 00:10:35.234
that Santos actually turned himself

00:10:35.234 --> 00:10:38.371
in to the FBI office in Melville New York

00:10:38.371 --> 00:10:39.905
and was then taken here

00:10:39.905 --> 00:10:41.073
to the federal courthouse.

00:10:41.073 --> 00:10:42.742
And that's why we didn't actually see him

00:10:42.742 --> 00:10:44.143
drive up and go in.

00:10:44.143 --> 00:10:45.811
But he is in custody right now.

00:10:45.811 --> 00:10:47.279
We do expect him to go

00:10:47.279 --> 00:10:49.315
before a judge on these 13 charges.

00:10:49.315 --> 00:10:50.750
It's unclear of that timing

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:51.417
as of now,

00:10:51.417 --> 00:10:53.586
but a pretty strong statement there

00:10:53.853 --> 00:10:54.954
from the DOJ.

